==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 2~8 seconds<sup>60f~240f</sup>.
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 0.27~0.67 seconds<sup>8f~20f</sup>.
**1 [[Otta-smack-u]] spawns.
**1 [[Otta-smack-u]] spawns.
**1 [[Otta-smack-u]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 14~26.67 seconds<sup>420f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Since THE SLOTH only spawns on base hit, it is heavily advised that you kill Master A. before hitting the base, lest you want to deal with 2 backliners at once. Units with high health like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] can break through Master A's constant attacks. Once he's dead, make sure you kill the Celeboodles and Otta-smack-us before they can wreak too much havoc on your frontline. [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] can deal with them quickly. Beware that THE SLOTH will end them, but they can do good damage before then. The only enemies that spawn after the initial wave are Those Guys and Otta-smack-u, so you can just chip at THE SLOTH and send high-damage units to take care of the Ottas.

